Great! Now let me verify that all tests pass:
Perfect! All tests are now passing. 

The bug was an off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was returning `parts[1]` (the second element of the split array) instead of `parts[0]` (the first element). This caused:
1. `test_basic` to fail: returned 'world' instead of 'hello'
2. `test_single` to error: IndexError when trying to access index 1 of a single-element list

The fix was simple: change `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]`. All tests now pass successfully.
